      "note": [
        "Note that the table for transport emissions currently only includes emissions from road transports. The environmental accounts statistics on air emissions are calculated with a production perspective and cover direct emissions from Swedish economic actors, regardless of the geographical location of the emissions. The production perspective differs from the territorial perspective (used for emissions inventories as reported to the UNFCCC) which covers all emissions arising inside Sweden´s border. Much of the source data used to produce the environmental accounts statistics on air emissions are produced with a territorial perspective. In order to adjust for the difference between the environmental accounts production perspective and the territorial perspective of source data, a so-called residence adjustment is applied. It is applied primarily for transport-related emissions. More information about the calculation method and source data used for the residence adjustment is available in the quality declaration for the statistics (in Swedish only).",
        "Correction 2025-02-11: Data have been corrected.",
        "The statistics on regional production-based air emissions are no longer updated. Similar statistics are available in the National Emissions Database, where Sweden’s territorial air emissions are reported by county and municipality (in Swedish only).  \r\n[the Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute – the National Emissions Database](https://nationellaemissionsdatabasen.smhi.se)"
